      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "We compared d-tubocurarine and rocuronium for the prevention of succinylcholine-induced fasciculations and postoperative myalgia (POM) and evaluated the influence of both drugs on the speed of onset and recovery of succinylcholine."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Seventy-five women undergoing surgery of short duration were studied. They were randomized to one of three groups: group SAL received normal saline followed three minutes later by 1.0 mg.kg-1 succinylcholine; group ROC received 0.05 mg.kg-1 rocuronium + 1.5 mg.kg-1 succinylcholine; group DTC received 0.05 mg.kg-1 d-tubocurarine + 1.5 mg.kg-1 succinylcholine. Single-twitch stimulation was applied to the ulnar nerve every 10 sec and the EMG response of the adductor pollicis was recorded. Fasciculations were assessed by a blinded observer on a scale of 0-3. Patients were asked 24 and 48 hr later to rate POM using a scale of 0-10."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The interval needed for twitch height to decrease to 10% of initial value after succinylcholine was longer in group ROC (58 +/- 20 sec) (mean +/- SD) compared with group SAL (44 +/- 13 sec) (P < 0.05). Recovery to 20% occurred faster in group ROC (324 +/- 83 sec) than in groups SAL (456 +/- 103 sec) and DTC (450 +/-132 sec) (P < 0.05). Fasciculations were more intense in groups SAL than in groups ROC and DTC (P < 0.001). Patients rated POM as less intense 24hr postoperatively only in group ROC (1.2 +/- 2.4) compared with group SAL (3.3 +/- 3.5) (P < 0.05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Rocuronium prevents succinylcholine-induced fasciculations and POM. Rocuronium also delays the onset of succinylcholine and shortens its duration compared with d-tubocurarine."
        }
      ]},
